---
import AppShell from '../../layouts/AppShell.astro';
---

<AppShell mode="public"
  title="VS Code integration — LoopSkill Docs"
  description="Three ways to use LoopSkill inside VS Code: Continue extension, Cline extension, and Claude Code CLI in the integrated terminal."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-24">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Docs · VS Code</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">
      VS Code integration
    </h1>
    <p class="text-muted text-lg leading-relaxed mb-12">
      Three paths to get LoopSkill working inside VS Code. Pick the one that matches your
      setup — they all give your agent the same six tools.
    </p>

    <!-- Path A: Continue -->
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mb-2">Path A — Continue extension</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mb-5">
      <a href="https://continue.dev" class="text-accent hover:opacity-80 underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Continue</a>
      is an open-source AI coding assistant that supports MCP. Add LoopSkill as an MCP server in
      Continue's config file.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted-soft mb-2">
      File: <code class="text-xs bg-bg-elev rounded px-1">~/.continue/config.json</code>
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-[#0d0d0d] border border-border rounded-xl p-4 text-sm text-text overflow-x-auto mb-5"><code>&#123;
  "mcpServers": [
    &#123;
      "name": "loopskill",
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/loopskill-mcp/loopskill_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": &#123; "RECIPES_API_KEY": "rec_live_your_key_here" &#125;
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>

    <div class="aspect-video bg-bg-elev rounded-xl mb-2 flex items-center justify-center">
      <span class="text-sm text-muted-soft">Screenshot: Continue MCP settings panel with LoopSkill server added</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted-soft mb-10 text-center">Continue's MCP config panel — screenshots arriving soon.</p>

    <!-- Path B: Cline -->
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mb-2">Path B — Cline extension</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mb-5">
      <a href="https://github.com/cline/cline" class="text-accent hover:opacity-80 underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cline</a>
      (formerly Claude Dev) has a built-in MCP settings panel. Same JSON shape as Continue — just
      drop it into Cline's MCP configuration dialog.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted-soft mb-2">
      Open the Cline panel → gear icon → <strong>MCP Servers</strong> → <strong>Edit Configuration</strong>.
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-[#0d0d0d] border border-border rounded-xl p-4 text-sm text-text overflow-x-auto mb-5"><code>&#123;
  "mcpServers": &#123;
    "loopskill": &#123;
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/loopskill-mcp/loopskill_mcp_server.py"],
      "env": &#123;
        "RECIPES_API_KEY": "rec_live_your_key_here"
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

    <div class="aspect-video bg-bg-elev rounded-xl mb-2 flex items-center justify-center">
      <span class="text-sm text-muted-soft">Screenshot: Cline MCP settings with LoopSkill configured</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted-soft mb-10 text-center">Cline MCP configuration panel — screenshots arriving soon.</p>

    <!-- Path C: Claude Code CLI -->
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mb-2">Path C — Claude Code CLI in VS Code terminal</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mb-5">
      If you run <a href="https://claude-code.nousresearch.com/docs" class="text-accent hover:opacity-80 underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Claude Code</a>
      inside VS Code's integrated terminal, the <code class="text-xs bg-bg-elev rounded px-1">install the loopskill skill</code>
      flow works exactly the same as in any other terminal — no MCP server config needed.
    </p>

    <ol class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-5 text-sm text-muted">
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-none w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">1</span>
        <div>
          <p>Open VS Code's integrated terminal: <kbd class="text-xs bg-bg-elev border border-border rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">Ctrl+`</kbd> (or <kbd class="text-xs bg-bg-elev border border-border rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">⌃`</kbd> on Mac).</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-none w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">2</span>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <p>Start Claude Code:</p>
          <pre class="bg-[#0d0d0d] border border-border rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-text overflow-x-auto mt-2"><code>claude</code></pre>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-none w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">3</span>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <p>Install the LoopSkill meta-skill once per agent directory:</p>
          <pre class="bg-[#0d0d0d] border border-border rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-text overflow-x-auto mt-2"><code>curl -sL https://app.loopskill.io/skill -o ~/.claude/skills/loopskill/SKILL.md</code></pre>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-none w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">4</span>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <p>Your agent now has marketplace awareness. Ask it to search or install any skill:</p>
          <pre class="bg-[#0d0d0d] border border-border rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-text overflow-x-auto mt-2"><code>Search the LoopSkill marketplace for an SEO audit skill and install it.</code></pre>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="aspect-video bg-bg-elev rounded-xl mb-2 flex items-center justify-center">
      <span class="text-sm text-muted-soft">Screenshot: Claude Code running in VS Code integrated terminal with loopskill installed</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted-soft mb-10 text-center">Claude Code in VS Code terminal — screenshots arriving soon.</p>

    <!-- Which to pick -->
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mb-4">Which path should I use?</h2>
    <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-10">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-text font-semibold">If you use…</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-text font-semibold">Use path</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Continue as your AI assistant</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-text font-medium">A — Continue MCP</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Cline as your AI assistant</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-text font-medium">B — Cline MCP</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted">Claude Code CLI in any terminal</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-text font-medium">C — integrated terminal</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-2xl flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-text">Using Cursor instead?</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Cursor uses the same MCP JSON shape as Claude Desktop. See the MCP setup doc.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/docs/mcp" class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm font-semibold border border-border hover:border-accent text-text transition">
        MCP setup →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</AppShell>
